2,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Todd Monken"},{"season":2024,"team":"BAL","distance":0.6992,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Todd Monken"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"CLE","distance":0.6769,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"CLE","distance":0.758,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"DET","distance":0.9167,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"},{"season":2023,"team":"DET","distance":0.9282,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"},{"season":2024,"team":"DET","distance":0.9742,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Buccaneers are 3-5 through week 8 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 178 to 151. The defense has done most of the work, ranking 2nd in EPA allowed while the offense sits 27th in EPA per play. What sets them apart is the lowest pass rate and the highest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Buccaneers offense has struggled, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. They have been one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Baker Mayfield has run the passing game, with Emeka Egbuka leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Buccaneers have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 5th or better in all five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per play, where it ranks 2nd, and its weakest has been sack rate, where it ranks 24th. YaYa Diaby has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is David Walker, who has 4 sacks while playing only 37% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they have the highest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Buccaneers have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 17% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 100% of field goals, which is the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the offensive line, about 26% of the money on the books.","players":"Baker Mayfield has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 679 yards. Emeka Egbuka has been the clear top target with 24% of the looks and 240 receiving yards. Bucky Irving has handled most of the work in the backfield with 64% of the carries. On defense, David Walker leads the team with 4 sacks and Alex Anzalone has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Zac Robinson is calling the offense and Todd Bowles is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Bears and the 2022 Commanders. Their defense looks most like the 2023 and 2024 Browns.","trends":"The offense went from 20th in EPA per play in 2025 to 27th so far this season, a modest decline. The defense moved from 17th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 2nd so far this season, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 20% to 0%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}